NOTES ON JOINS 


RIGHT AND LEFT JOINS 

## Mental Model

Think in terms of "which table is preserved":

LEFT JOIN → preserve left table  
RIGHT JOIN → preserve right table  

Instead of remembering both, focus on:
"Which table do I want to preserve?"


  
LEFT JOIN and RIGHT JOIN are mirror operations.                                               
                                                                                      
A RIGHT JOIN can always be rewritten as a LEFT JOIN by swapping table positions.      
So in practice, mastering LEFT JOIN is sufficient for most use cases.                 


  
## Equivalence Example

  -- RIGHT JOIN
SELECT *
FROM A
RIGHT JOIN B
ON A.id = B.id;

-- Equivalent LEFT JOIN
SELECT *
FROM B
LEFT JOIN A
ON A.id = B.id;


## Why This Works

LEFT JOIN → keeps all rows from the left table  
RIGHT JOIN → keeps all rows from the right table  

So:
A RIGHT JOIN B  ≡  B LEFT JOIN A
